{#
  Primary navigation.

  With MAW Menus installed and a menu of this name built, that menu is rendered. Otherwise the automatic
  page tree (partials/navigation-auto.html.twig) — the behaviour every maw-starter site had before 1.5.0.

  maw_menu_exists() rather than a length check on maw_menu(): a menu that exists but is empty is a
  deliberate choice to show nothing, and must not silently fall back to the page tree.

  `depth: 2` is a hard clamp. css/layout.css opens submenus with `.nav-list ul` positioned at
  `top: 100%; left: 0` on hover/:focus-within, with no JS — a third level would have no positioning rule
  and be unreachable on touch. Deeper menus need a flyout, which is a theme change.
#}
{# Empty means "whichever menu the plugin calls the main one", so that choice lives in one place. #}
{% set menu_name = theme_var('header.menu')|default('') %}

{% if maw_menu_exists(menu_name) %}
    {% include 'partials/menu.html.twig' with {
        nodes: maw_menu(menu_name),
        class: 'nav-list',
        depth: 2
    } only %}
{% else %}
    {% include 'partials/navigation-auto.html.twig' %}
{% endif %}
